{"abstract":"This article offers an intermedial analysis of how books are represented in The Witcher 3, building on the media theories of Lars Elleström and W. J. T. Mitchell. The analysis shows how the game pits books against images and exposes latent tensions in the representational conventions of games. The game reflects an intermedial excess that speaks to a more profound crisis in the discursive construction of the computer games medium. Building on the analysis, the article turns to discuss how the medium of computer games is qualified through both its likenesses and differences to other narrative media, most notably literature and cinema. Compared to these media, computer games entice their players with promises of immersion and control, while ultimately failing to fulfil both. The intermedial excess of The Witcher 3 can be understood as a playful commentary on the promises and limits to the representational capacities of computer games.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-792311"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff"],"keyword":["Books","Games","Intermediality","Representation"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Embargoed Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the bookworm of blaviken an intermedial analysis of books in the witcher 000000000003 wild hunt","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.intellectbooks.com/journal-of-gaming-virtual-worlds","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-792311","identifier":[{"id":"85213436800","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-fd031222-96bc-4108-afa9-8f596781d97f"],"keyword":["Books","Games","Intermediality","representation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CE26984C496539096838AF42790622E7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"ea","embargo":"2025-11-30","type":"loc","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Design, Media and Educational Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"7989dd33-d458-476d-83c7-9bf0b5ae16d8","name":"Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","orcid":"0000-0001-8217-6058","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1386/jgvw_00102_1","issn":["1757191X","17571928"],"issn_org":["1757191X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Gaming & Virtual Worlds","pages":"257-275","publisher":"Intellect","status":"p","title":"Journal of Gaming & Virtual Worlds","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85213436800"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-fd031222-96bc-4108-afa9-8f596781d97f"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The bookworm of Blaviken : an intermedial analysis of books in The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-792311","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This paper considers designers’ embodied engagements while designing for play from the lens of “care.” We consider such engagements as socio-material relations of care, following recent theorizations of care within care studies. Relying on observations from a variety of activities undertaken by students during a two-week design workshop on embodied play design, we present a theoretical model that identifies two orders of care in design activities: First order, “care through,” indexes the immediate objects that designers attend to in the here-and-now while implementing procedures, practices and tools provided by diverse design methods. Second order, “care forward,” indicates the future beneficiaries of designed things, who are typically, though not necessarily, the projected users of design. The paper contributes to design literature by providing a model for investigating the affective and practical relations of care in design practice, with implications for how specific design activities and methods frame care.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","Kaygan, Harun"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-750314"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-28","place":"Boston, us","start":"2024-06-24","title":"Design Research Society International Conference 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff"],"keyword":["CARE","Design for Play","Design process","STS"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"feelings about the other body caring through and forward in design for play","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/drs.2024.776","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-750314","ids":["sdu-34cdcdfd-166d-46e9-9261-0a1cc80d82e5"],"keyword":["STS","body-centred design methods","care","design for play","design process"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-09057E6D41B9DB85979EA99D3BFD40C8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/264659896/_Feelings_about_the_other_body_caring_through_and_forward_In_de.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/drs.2024.776","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Design, Media and Educational Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"7989dd33-d458-476d-83c7-9bf0b5ae16d8","name":"Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","orcid":"0000-0001-8217-6058","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Harun","key":"kayganpau","last":"Kaygan","locid":"0e6c26df-6011-4ed8-9aee-a68094a1fbcb","name":"Kaygan, Harun","orcid":"0000-0002-6460-3092","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"C.","key":"graypedh","last":"Gray","name":"Gray, C.","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"P.","key":"hekkertpedh","last":"Hekkert","name":"Hekkert, P.","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"L.","key":"forlanopedh","last":"Forlano","name":"Forlano, L.","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"P.","key":"ciuccarellipedh","last":"Ciuccarelli","name":"Ciuccarelli, P.","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.21606/drs.2024.776","place":"Boston","publisher":"Design Research Society","status":"p","subtitle":"Boston","title":"DRS 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-34cdcdfd-166d-46e9-9261-0a1cc80d82e5"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"“Feelings about the other body” : Caring through and forward in design for play","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-750314","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Design approaches in the last two decades have shown extensive interest in and developed diverse strategies for taking users’ bodily capabilities and embodied experiences into account both within the design process and in the design outcomes. This workshop focuses on one specific way in which users’ bodies have been characterized and addressed by design practice across such diverse approaches as wearable technologies, design for self-tracking, somadesign, etc.: ‘the deep body.’ In this context, ‘the deep body’ refers to the various manners in which design activities engage with users’ bodies with the consideration that they possess an internal dimension, whether literal or metaphorical, that can be explored through embodied design. Based on this definition, the workshop will actively engage participants in a collaborative exploration of the now and future of ‘deep bodies’ in design. We will utilize presentations, discussions and embodied and speculative ideation and so build a collection of fictional abstracts that outline design approaches and outcomes, and practice-oriented definitions for considering the ‘depth’ of the body.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kaygan, Harun","Genç, Çağlar","Buruk, Oğuz","Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","Kristupas Gabrielaitis, Linas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-766119"],"event":{"end":"2024-10-11","place":"Tampere, fi","start":"2024-10-04","title":"Mindtrek '24","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Kaygan, Harun"],"country":["Finland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Tampere University"],"keyword":["Embodied design","Fictional abstracts","Speculative design"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the deep body exploring users insides through design fiction","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85208200722","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-766119","identifier":[{"id":"85208200722","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-76249f73-8e04-46e9-8236-f7cfc41d3fba"],"keyword":["body-centred design","embodied design","fictional abstracts","speculative design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E6E02CECF6EFD9617B66AB094FBB9CB0"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Design, Media and Educational Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fi","key":"tampere university","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Tampere University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Harun","key":"kayganpau","last":"Kaygan","locid":"0e6c26df-6011-4ed8-9aee-a68094a1fbcb","name":"Kaygan, Harun","orcid":"0000-0002-6460-3092","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Çağlar","key":"gençpau","last":"Genç","name":"Genç, Çağlar","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Oğuz","key":"burukpau","last":"Buruk","name":"Buruk, Oğuz","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"7989dd33-d458-476d-83c7-9bf0b5ae16d8","name":"Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","orcid":"0000-0001-8217-6058","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Linas","key":"kristupasgabrielaitispau","last":"Kristupas Gabrielaitis","name":"Kristupas Gabrielaitis, Linas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3681716.3681743","eisbn":["9798400718236"],"pages":"325-329","place":"New York","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 27th International Academic Mindtrek Conference","title":"Mindtrek '24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85208200722"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-76249f73-8e04-46e9-8236-f7cfc41d3fba"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The Deep Body : Exploring users’ insides through design fiction","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-766119","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In design for children's play, the user's body occupies a central position, not only because of the ever-changing bodily dimensions and skills of child users but because play is seen as a key driver of children's development. Based on interviews with professionals in play design, this article analyzes how designers figure the child user's body as being in the making. I identified three figures: the biological body in early childhood development, the potentially unhealthy body of profiled children, and the child as embodied subjectivity in the making. I discuss how these figures become central in how designers imagine the value created by play design as well as their implications on design. This article presents my findings that play designers imagine their design work to create value by stimulating the child's neurodevelopment, activating profiled unhealthy bodies in high-intensity play, and even forming subjectivities through embodied experiences of mastery and control. Although the analysis focuses on design for play, the article contributes to our overall understanding of how contemporary design relates to its users and strives to improve their health and well-being. Therefore, the article discusses its findings in relation to two themes: twentieth-century biopolitics and design for care.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-791884"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff"],"keyword":["Child Development","Health","Play Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"we cultivate children s skillsets figurations of the user s body in design for play","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.sheji.2024.11.005","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-791884","identifier":[{"id":"85212344143","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-6ba6088d-dd7a-4701-9e60-16fb50da8d09"],"keyword":["child development","health","play design","user's body"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-67476530062B0C7B1B13DD8B6C8C0370"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.sheji.2024.11.005","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/281259895/Open_access_version.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Design, Media and Educational Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ida Kathrine","key":"hammeleffjørgensenpau","last":"Hammeleff Jørgensen","locid":"7989dd33-d458-476d-83c7-9bf0b5ae16d8","name":"Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","name_org":"Hammeleff Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine","orcid":"0000-0001-8217-6058","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.sheji.2024.11.005","issn":["24058718","24058726"],"issn_org":["24058726"],"issue":"4","journal":"She Ji","pages":"474-493","publisher":"Tongji University Press","status":"p","title":"She Ji","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85212344143"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-6ba6088d-dd7a-4701-9e60-16fb50da8d09"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"“We cultivate children's skillsets” : figurations of the user's body in design for play","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-791884","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This paper offers an analysis of how design activities engage with the body in the context of teaching embodied methods, and specifically body-centric design for play. Based on the analysis, we propose an empirically grounded framework for describing the various engagements with and considerations around the body as it comes into play in coursework on the use of body-centric design methods. Under an overarching interest in dealing with use contexts and interactions as embodied and situated experiences, designers have been concerned with diverse issues, problems, aspects and opportunities related to the body. In interaction design and design-oriented HCI, this is reflected in a wealth of theories, design concepts, methodological frameworks and design examples that describe, explore and guide the design of body-technology relations. Much of such work has been of a normative character, recommending how design practice or designed things should relate to bodies, with an eye to method or design concept development. Few work has been concerned with how this interest can be implemented in design education, and how to teach students to attune themselves to bodies. In this paper, we apply an analytical, rather than normative, approach to body-centric methods, and one that is situated within the context of a specific area of interest for design practice, i.e. that of design for play. Through that, we focus on how distinct views of and approaches to body intersect in design activities, as they are carried out by students as part of coursework. The paper also contributes to embodied play design education by providing a body-centred framework. Based on empirical data collected from project work carried out by design students on a master’s course in product design, this paper offers an analysis of the students’ engagements with and considerations of the body.We find five bodily dimensions: the physical body and its parts; the body as locus of action; the body as locus of embodied experience; the social body; the body as materially entangled – and one practice-specific dimension, the body in play. These findings are then described in the form of a matrix aimed at guiding design education.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","Kaygan, Harun"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-733658"],"event":{"end":"2024-02-14","place":"Cork, ie","start":"2024-02-11","title":"Tangible Embedded and Embodied Interaction","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Kaygan, Harun"],"keyword":["Design education","Design for Play","Embodiment"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the body in play dimensions of embodiment in design for play","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/245696989/J_rgensen_Kaygan_The_body_in_play_AM.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-733658","identifier":[{"id":"85185217899","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-36f12369-4594-41f8-a1bc-92ca58e058f8"],"keyword":["body-centered design","design education","design for play","embodiment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8804B1AB6622F8B7BA9103ECFF506927"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/245696989/J_rgensen_Kaygan_The_body_in_play_AM.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Design, Media and Educational Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"7989dd33-d458-476d-83c7-9bf0b5ae16d8","name":"Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","orcid":"0000-0001-8217-6058","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Harun","key":"kayganpau","last":"Kaygan","locid":"0e6c26df-6011-4ed8-9aee-a68094a1fbcb","name":"Kaygan, Harun","orcid":"0000-0002-6460-3092","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3623509.3633379","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"ACM International Conference on Tangible, Embedded and Embodied Interaction","title":"TEI’24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85185217899"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-36f12369-4594-41f8-a1bc-92ca58e058f8"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The Body in Play : Dimensions of Embodiment in Design for Play","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-733658","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This chapter considers computer games as a qualified medium situated in an intermedial network of other qualified, technical media and media cultures. The aim of this chapter is to offer an overview of state-of-the-art research, which in four different ways sheds light on the relations between games and other media, supports intermedial analysis of computer games, and informs our understanding of computer games as a qualified medium that favors certain modes of expression, technologies, content matter, and modes of use. The chapter offers a broad review of literature originating in the field of game studies and studies of games and gaming technologies from the fields of media studies. This research is categorized into four different categories (comprising four parts of the review), each dealing with a different aspect of the intermedial network in which the qualified medium of computer games is situated. Part one concerns existing theoretical approaches to computer games as a distinct formal mode of expression along with critiques of such approaches. Part two reviews research that considers the content of games through the lens of adaptation, transmedial storytelling, and convergence culture. Part three discusses media historical and archeological approaches to the technical media and platforms employed by games. Finally, part four is concerned with empirical studies on games as a media culture that is practiced through the means of other qualified media (such as cinema and film, fanfiction, and play guides).","author_count":4,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-671875"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the qualified medium of computer games form and matter technology and use","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-671875","ids":["sdu-cd9a836d-7721-43d0-92f8-a8ed84a31fb3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-B98128694CAFC43B37DF1CEB3C226B4B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Design, Media and Educational Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"7989dd33-d458-476d-83c7-9bf0b5ae16d8","name":"Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","orcid":"0000-0001-8217-6058","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jørgen","key":"bruhnpedh","last":"Bruhn","name":"Bruhn, Jørgen","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Asun","key":"lópezvarelaazcáratepedh","last":"López-Varela Azcárate","name":"López-Varela Azcárate, Asun","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Miriam","key":"depaivavieirapedh","last":"de Paiva Vieira","name":"de Paiva Vieira, Miriam","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-91263-5_47-1","eisbn":["9783030912635"],"isbn":["9783030912635"],"publisher":"Palgrave Macmillan","status":"p","title":"The Palgrave handbook of intermediality"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-cd9a836d-7721-43d0-92f8-a8ed84a31fb3"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The qualified medium of computer games : form and matter, technology, and use","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-671875","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Widespread engagement of design practice with societal challenges have meant that care appears more and more often as a design objective in diverse contexts such as design for healthcare, design for sustainability and social design. This paper explores the role of design process in directing designers’ affective interest and efforts at different aspects of the body, asking how specific methods and tools mediate care, including what is being cared for and through what means. We use research through and into design process, based on data from a two-week design workshop on body-centered methods for design for play. Drawing on our analysis, we present a theoretical model that identifies two orders of care in design process: First-order care – “care-through” – indexes the immediate objects that designers attend to while implementing procedures, practices and tools provided by diverse design methods. Second-order care – “care-for” – indicates the beneficiaries of designed things, who are typically, though not necessarily, the projected users of design. Objects of the first order – specific body parts and bodily capabilities, sensations, or specific relations between bodies, etc. – act as the basis for designers’ attunement to their users for instituting second-order care. The model expands the notion of care in design research, emphasizing that care is present in the practical knowledge work carried out by designers, thus bridging considerations of designing with care and designing for care. The paper aims to create greater dialogue between design research and the now-established empirical and theoretical interest in care within STS.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","Kaygan, Harun"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-684964"],"event":{"end":"2023-06-09","place":"Oslo, no","start":"2023-06-07","title":"6th Nordic STS Conference 2023","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff"],"keyword":["CARE","Design for Play","Methods","STS"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"caring through and for in design for play","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-684964","ids":["sdu-0927d626-5d20-4f70-96b1-48f2554bb7b7"],"keyword":["STS","care","design for play","methods"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4D2EE8846AADBB4EBD47B6C2C690AB27"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Design, Media and Educational Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"7989dd33-d458-476d-83c7-9bf0b5ae16d8","name":"Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","orcid":"0000-0001-8217-6058","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Harun","key":"kayganpau","last":"Kaygan","locid":"0e6c26df-6011-4ed8-9aee-a68094a1fbcb","name":"Kaygan, Harun","orcid":"0000-0002-6460-3092","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-0927d626-5d20-4f70-96b1-48f2554bb7b7"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Caring through and for in design for play","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://