{"abstract":"ow we talk about a medium reveals a lot about who we consider its target audience or user and what purposes we attribute to their engagement with the medium. The public discourse on digital games in both Europe and North America, have for many years been characterized by the idea, that digital games was, roughly speaking, for young, teenage boys, who spend hours upon hours painted by the luminescence of the computer screen and immersed in mindless entertainment. This was of course never true.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384360"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Audience Perception","Cultural Representation in Gaming","Digital Games Discourse","Gaming Stereotypes","Media Engagement"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards more responsible representational practices in games","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://gamegeneration.or.kr/board/post/view?match=id:86","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384360","ids":["itu-d24bb672-88af-4023-b4e3-9c031a48efb4"],"keyword":["Audience Perception","Cultural Representation in Gaming","Digital Games Discourse","Gaming Stereotypes","Media Engagement"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1C15D72CEF5533C8D360B600CE05DB2C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://gamegeneration.or.kr/board/post/view?match=id:86","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["itu-d24bb672-88af-4023-b4e3-9c031a48efb4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards more responsible representational practices in games","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384360","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"This paper aims to examine the uses of commercial, digital games within the classroom. Our focus is on commercial games rather than on games designed specifically for educational purposes. This study review existing attempts of using digital, commercial games in the classroom.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","Debus, Michael S."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383988"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Classroom use","Commercial games","Digital Games","Educational technology","Game based learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"not just fun and games the status quo of commercial games in teaching","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.36253/978-88-5518-412-0","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383988","ids":["itu-b9e10739-8b6a-4181-8969-61c253db35c3"],"keyword":["Classroom use","Commercial games","Digital games","Educational technology","Game-based learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-ED9A27F4B32839928FD2EF003A3E2B96"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.36253/978-88-5518-412-0","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","key":"jørgensen